    editorial_html: `<p>Black Desert Online represents the worst-case scenario for MMO monetization—direct pay-to-progression tied to gear enhancement with hidden odds and no pity system. The system creates absolute power gaps where spending directly translates to competitive advantage, making skill irrelevant compared to gear investment.</p><p>The hidden success rates for enhancement combined with lack of transparency about actual odds make the system impossible for players to evaluate before spending. This is gambling disguised as legitimate progression mechanics.</p><p>Black Desert Online should be avoided unless you accept free-to-play status and permanent second-class competitive standing. The monetization is among the most predatory in all MMO gaming. Free players are not competing with spenders; they're accepting a completely different game experience.</p>`,
